---
import ContentLayout from "../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import RelatedLinks from "../../components/RelatedLinks.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import TrustBlock from "../../components/TrustBlock.astro";
import { editorialTeam, carTrustPoints } from "../../data/editorial";

const title = "VW Tiguan II facelift service schedule and intervals";
const description =
  "A practical service-interval guide to the 2020-2024 VW Tiguan II facelift, including which maintenance items should stay on schedule and which ones deserve earlier attention.";
const intro =
  "The late Mk2 Tiguan does not need an exotic maintenance routine, but it does punish owners who stretch the basics and then act surprised when the car feels rougher, hotter, or less predictable. This guide is here to keep the service rhythm realistic: what needs regular timing, what short-trip use accelerates, and which jobs are cheaper when they are done before the complaint starts.";
const modifiedTime = new Date("2026-04-16");
const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: "Home", href: "/" },
  { label: "Guides", href: "/guides/" },
  { label: title }
];
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Does the facelift Tiguan need a strict service schedule?",
    answer:
      "Yes. The maintenance pattern is not unusually complex, but oil, brake, battery, and coolant-related neglect change how the car feels faster than many owners expect."
  },
  {
    question: "What service item gets stretched too often on this Tiguan?",
    answer:
      "Oil changes and brake-service timing are the two most common places owners get casual, especially when the car does mostly short trips."
  },
  {
    question: "Should short-trip use change the service rhythm?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Short-trip use is harder on oil condition, battery reserve, and brake cleanliness, so the practical maintenance pace often needs to tighten up."
  }
];

const relatedProblems = [
  { href: "/problems/oil-level-drops-between-services/", title: "Oil level drops between services", description: "Open this when the service schedule question is already drifting toward oil-consumption or top-up territory.", eyebrow: "Problem guide" },
  { href: "/problems/battery-struggles-after-short-trips/", title: "Battery struggles after short trips", description: "Use this when service timing and daily-use pattern are starting to overlap.", eyebrow: "Problem guide" },
  { href: "/problems/car-shakes-when-braking/", title: "Car shakes when braking", description: "A useful next read when delayed brake service is starting to become a real drivability complaint.", eyebrow: "Problem guide" }
];

const relatedBest = [
  { href: "/best/best-engine-oil-for-vw-tiguan-2020/", title: "Best engine oil for VW Tiguan 2020", description: "Use this when the schedule says oil service matters now and the next question is what to fill it with.", eyebrow: "Engine Oil" },
  { href: "/best/best-coolant-for-vw-tiguan-2020/", title: "Best coolant for VW Tiguan 2020", description: "Open this when coolant timing and fluid spec are the real maintenance question.", eyebrow: "Coolant" },
  { href: "/best/best-batteries-for-vw-tiguan-2020/", title: "Best batteries for VW Tiguan 2020", description: "Useful when short-trip use has already shortened the battery story.", eyebrow: "Batteries" },
  { href: "/best/best-brake-pads-for-vw-tiguan-2020/", title: "Best brake pads for VW Tiguan 2020", description: "Worth opening when service timing is catching up to normal Tiguan brake wear.", eyebrow: "Brake Pads" }
];

const relatedGuides = [
  { href: "/guides/vw-tiguan-ii-facelift-maintenance-costs-and-weak-points/", title: "VW Tiguan II facelift maintenance costs and weak points", description: "Use this when the service rhythm question becomes a budget and weak-point question too.", eyebrow: "Maintenance guide" },
  { href: "/guides/vw-tiguan-ii-facelift-common-problems/", title: "VW Tiguan II facelift common problems", description: "Open this if the service schedule is already colliding with a repeat complaint.", eyebrow: "Ownership guide" }
];
---

<ContentLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  intro={intro}
  image="/images/photos/cars/vw-tiguan-2020.webp"
  modifiedTime={modifiedTime}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  faqs={faqs}
  editorialSummary="This guide is written as a practical service-interval and maintenance timing overview for the facelift Tiguan, with emphasis on the jobs that actually shape ownership quality."
  editorialByline={`By ${editorialTeam.name}`}
  editorialReviewedLabel={`Reviewed ${modifiedTime.toLocaleDateString("en-US", { month: "short", day: "numeric", year: "numeric" })}`}
  editorialBadges={["Service guide", "Generation-specific", "Interval-focused"]}
>
  <TrustBlock
    title="How to use this guide"
    summary="Use this page when the real question is not just what breaks, but how to keep a facelift Tiguan from sliding into the same predictable complaints in the first place."
    byline={`By ${editorialTeam.name}`}
    checkedLabel={`Checked ${modifiedTime.toLocaleDateString("en-US", { month: "short", day: "numeric", year: "numeric" })}`}
    points={carTrustPoints}
  />

  <Section title="The short version" intro="If you only need the quick maintenance read, start here.">
    <ul class="grid gap-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Oil service, brake service, battery condition, and coolant monitoring are the big timing items that shape how sorted this Tiguan feels.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Short-trip use justifies a more conservative oil-and-battery mindset than a highway-driven example.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">The expensive mistake is treating “still drives fine” as proof the maintenance interval can keep stretching.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Core service rhythm" intro="These are the service areas that deserve routine attention even before the car starts complaining.">
    <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">Oil service</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Do not stretch it just because the car still feels normal</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Oil-service delay is one of the easiest ways to make the ownership story rougher than it needs to be, especially on short-trip cars.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">Brake service</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Brake timing matters before the pedal feels bad</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Waiting until vibration or roughness is obvious is how ordinary Tiguan brake work turns into a second repair cycle.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">Battery reserve</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Short trips compress the battery schedule</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">The maintenance interval here is less about mileage and more about how the car is used day to day.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">Coolant checks</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Treat slow drift like a service signal, not background noise</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">Small coolant changes are often cheap early and annoying later. The interval mindset matters here.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="When to shorten the interval" intro="Real use pattern matters more than the optimistic service fantasy.">
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Mostly short trips, frequent cold starts, and long idle time justify a tighter oil and battery rhythm.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Stop-and-go use and repeated wet-weather driving justify more disciplined brake inspection and cleanup.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">If a small coolant issue is already showing up, the right move is earlier confirmation, not longer observation.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Where owners get the schedule wrong" intro="These are the service-interval mistakes that create the most unnecessary repair cost later.">
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-steel">
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Waiting for obvious drivability changes before handling plug, coil, or oil-related maintenance properly.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Treating battery complaints like a random surprise instead of a maintenance pattern tied to use case.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Letting brake service become reactive instead of preventive.</li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 px-4 py-3">Ignoring small fluid and cooling clues because the car still feels mostly fine.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <RelatedLinks title="Problem guides linked from this page" intro="Open these when the service timing question has already become a real complaint." items={relatedProblems} />
  <RelatedLinks title="Best-parts guides linked from this page" intro="Use these when the next step is turning interval timing into a practical parts shortlist." items={relatedBest} />
  <RelatedLinks title="Related ownership guides" intro="Open these when the service schedule is only one part of the broader Tiguan ownership picture." items={relatedGuides} />
</ContentLayout>
